==============================================================================
THE THREE CONSTRAINTS AS CURVES IN THE (A, phi) PLANE
==============================================================================
  measured m_mu/m_e      206.768282988 +- 4.50e-06   (21.8 ppb)
  booked point (sqrt2, 2/9) gives  206.770315973
  -> miss 9.83 ppm = 452 sigma  (cycle 8's headline)

==============================================================================
THE TRIANGLE: WHERE EACH PAIR OF CONSTRAINTS MEETS
==============================================================================
  vertex                                           A             phi
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  data x (A = sqrt2)                    1.4142135624    0.2222220471
  data x closure                        1.4142133251    0.2222221849
  (A = sqrt2) x closure  [booked]       1.4142135624    0.2222222222

  spread in A     2.373e-07   (0.168 ppm)
  spread in phi   1.751e-07   (0.788 ppm)

==============================================================================
THE SAME DISAGREEMENT, ONE VARIABLE AT A TIME
==============================================================================
  Grant the closure exactly, and let the light masses fix everything else:
    Q      = 0.666666554802      Q - 2/3 = -1.119e-07  (0.168 ppm)
    A      = 1.414213325073      A - sqrt2 = -2.373e-07

  Grant Q = 2/3 exactly instead, and do the same:
    phi    = 0.222222047098      phi - 2/9 = -1.751e-07  (0.788 ppm)

  So the conjunction fails, and this is the size of the failure. Whichever watch
  is granted, the other misses by well under one part per million. The 452 sigma
  measures how sharply m_mu/m_e is known, not how badly the sector is broken --
  a 9.8 ppm discrepancy on a 22 ppb measurement is unavoidably hundreds of sigma.
  Both readings are correct and neither alone is the whole statement.

==============================================================================
WHY THE TAU CANNOT SEE ANY OF THIS
==============================================================================
  the full three-mass point   A = 1.4142005052   phi = 0.2222296315
  its distance from the triangle:  dA = -1.306e-05   dphi = +7.409e-06
  the triangle's own size:         2.373e-07 in A, 1.751e-07 in phi

  The tau's +-0.12 MeV displaces the fitted point by 55x the triangle's width
  in A. That is the whole reason both watches sit under 1 sigma on a three-mass
  fit while their conjunction is dead on two: the tau's error bar is far larger
  than the structure being argued about, so it hides the disagreement rather
  than resolving it. Only the light masses can see the triangle at all.
